---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.extensions;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-website.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container prose-card">
    <p class="section-kicker">Build above shared meaning</p>
    <h2>Profiles, vendor layers, and business context</h2>
    <p>Core supplies a common investigative model. Public domain profiles add reviewed vocabulary, questions, and requirements. Vendor layers provide tooling and integrations. Business layers supply explicit policy, authority, thresholds, and organizational context.</p>
    <p>Each can specialize an investigation. None may silently redefine a Core outcome, change a question's proposition under the same identity, or turn a policy judgment into an observation.</p>

    <h2>Publish the semantic dependency</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Give profiles and extension definitions an identity and version.</li>
      <li>Declare constraints, dependencies, and whether an extension is required for interpretation.</li>
      <li>Expose unsupported required meaning instead of returning a misleading successful interpretation.</li>
      <li>Preserve unknown optional data when claiming lossless exchange.</li>
      <li>Use explicit binding parameters or a new definition identity when local behavior changes a question's meaning.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Follow the extension representation in the <a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/binding.md">candidate binding</a>. The logical proposal does not make arbitrary vendor key names interoperable.</p>

    <h2>Keep policy visible</h2>
    <p>A question about whether a tool call exceeded its permitted scope needs the relevant policy version and context. A risk score may support a decision if its scale, method, and interpretation are stated. A private score or hidden prompt cannot silently replace public assessment criteria.</p>
    <p>Record claimed authority separately from attribution. A human, agent, system, or organization label alone grants no permission. Importing a record neither authorizes an action nor permits access to referenced evidence.</p>

    <h2>Report exchange limits</h2>
    <p>A vendor-specific ticket layout may be optional display metadata. A dependency that changes the interpretation of a decision is not. When a recipient cannot interpret required semantics, its report must identify the affected content. When an export drops content, declare the loss.</p>
    <p><a href="/founding/01-core-contract.md">Read requirements TC-29 through TC-35</a> · <a href="/conformance/">Validation and exchange evidence</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
